  "question": "Does the source-emitted NDL frontend code and anonymous exact-child application state establish that target issue i25264793 is eligible for remote copying or expose a target-specific copy request object without login/request execution?",
  "answer": "No. Static inspection confirms that NDL Search globally implements remote-copy workflows and routes, including /request/rcopy/*, /request/cart, /api/cart, /api/request, /api/request/without-cart, /copy/remote and /help/remotecopy. The source code also shows an rcopy store whose request creation consumes already-populated requestItemFromTml/Ksk/Ilcl entries carrying fields such as cartItemId, rcopyPartItemId, itemId/risItemId, bibId and maximumFee. However, the anonymous exact-child state for i25264793 contains no populated target request/cart object: checkedCartItems is empty, requestCount is zero, and all three requestItemFrom* arrays are empty. These are default anonymous/client initial states, not a denial result. No source-emitted target-specific eligibility response, cart item, fee ceiling, request part ID or material-level request payload was obtained. No API contract was executed, no login occurred and no request was submitted.",
